(195235, 10813, 3585, '<td valign="top">Somebody offered us this anthurium plant at christmas, I was not too found of it, looks so artificially waxy, until it inspired me all kinds of more or less tastfull photographic ideas. Thanks for your critics and appreciation.</td>', 'Somebody offered us this anthurium plant at christmas, I was not too found of it, looks so artificially waxy, until it inspired me all kinds of more or less tastfull photographic ideas. Thanks for your critics and appreciation.', '2003-01-20 04:48:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(195240, 11013, 3540, '<td valign="top">Critique Club by Inspzil<br/> <br/>Composition - Well no job is finished until the paperwork is done.  Nothing is more true than those precious few moments of "dropping the kids off at the pool."  Being a veteran of 11th hour shots, I know how these things work.  The shower curtain as bright and colorful as it is, is really taking away from the subject of this pic.  The bright glare on the curtain is equally distracting.  It looks like the paper is tied on the subject.  I think it would''ve been more effective to just stuff it down there, plus stuffed a bunch more down there to make his backside all puffy with paper.  A little different perspective might''ve added to the mood of this too.  Maybe if you could''ve put the camera lower, like toilet level against the wall next to the toilet, taking the camera from the toilet''s perspective, you could''ve emphasized the paper a little more and taken some of the focus off the inside of the toilet and the shower curtain.  This is a good concept, but these 11th hour shots don''t afford us the time to hone this down and explore all of the options to make this shot as effective as it could be.<br/> <br/>Photography - This is a pretty well taken photo.  The only thing I don''t like is the flash on the shower curtain.  Exposure looks good as does DOF and focus.<br/> <br/>Processing - I don''t see anything standing out at me, so it must be good<br/> <br/>Overall - This shot has a lot of potential to be pretty good.  Some of the distracting things need to be removed or replaced.  A better angle on the shot would also minimize this stuff and concentrate our attentions to the humorous part of the photo.  Hope this can be of some help to you.  My best advice is take your photos prior to the 10th hour so you have a little time to rethink and reshoot them.  I should prolly listen to that advice myself!! - Bob</td>', 'Critique Club by Inspzil Composition - Well no job is finished until the paperwork is done.  Nothing is more true than those precious few moments of "dropping the kids off at the pool."  Being a veteran of 11th hour shots, I know how these things work.  The shower curtain as bright and colorful as it is, is really taking away from the subject of this pic.  The bright glare on the curtain is equally distracting.  It looks like the paper is tied on the subject.  I think it would''ve been more effective to just stuff it down there, plus stuffed a bunch more down there to make his backside all puffy with paper.  A little different perspective might''ve added to the mood of this too.  Maybe if you could''ve put the camera lower, like toilet level against the wall next to the toilet, taking the camera from the toilet''s perspective, you could''ve emphasized the paper a little more and taken some of the focus off the inside of the toilet and the shower curtain.  This is a good concept, but these 11th hour shots don''t afford us the time to hone this down and explore all of the options to make this shot as effective as it could be. Photography - This is a pretty well taken photo.  The only thing I don''t like is the flash on the shower curtain.  Exposure looks good as does DOF and focus. Processing - I don''t see anything standing out at me, so it must be good Overall - This shot has a lot of potential to be pretty good.  Some of the distracting things need to be removed or replaced.  A better angle on the shot would also minimize this stuff and concentrate our attentions to the humorous part of the photo.  Hope this can be of some help to you.  My best advice is take your photos prior to the 10th hour so you have a little time to rethink and reshoot them.  I should prolly listen to that advice myself!! - Bob', '2003-01-20 05:14:28.000000', NULL, 0),
